#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stefan Zipproth"
msgstr "Stefan Zipproth"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image src={stefan} alt=\"Stefan Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"
msgstr "<Image src={stefan} alt=\"Stefan Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Stefan Zipproth is the lead developer and creator of Ditana. A software "
"developer from St. Ursen, Switzerland, with a background in embedded systems "
"and cross-platform development. He has worked in industries ranging from RF "
"measurement and classical image processing to AI-powered medical imaging. "
"Since 2023, he has focused on developing and refining products for the Linux "
"ecosystem. A broader overview of his work — spanning systems architecture, "
"high-performance C++, and knowledge representation — is available on his "
"[personal portfolio](https://zipproth.ch)."
msgstr ""
"Stefan Zipproth es el desarrollador principal y creador de Ditana. "
"Desarrollador de software de St. Ursen (Suiza), con experiencia en sistemas "
"embebidos y desarrollo multiplataforma. Ha trabajado en sectores que van "
"desde la medición de RF y el procesamiento clásico de imágenes hasta la "
"imagen médica basada en IA. Desde 2023 se dedica a desarrollar y "
"perfeccionar productos para el ecosistema Linux. Hay una visión más amplia "
"de su trabajo —que abarca la arquitectura de sistemas, C++ de alto "
"rendimiento y la representación del conocimiento— en su [portafolio personal]"
"(https://zipproth.ch)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Through **acrion innovations GmbH**, Stefan manages the financial side of "
"Ditana while focusing solely on its development as a solo developer. This "
"structure ensures transparent stewardship of resources for the community-"
"driven project."
msgstr ""
"A través de **acrion innovations GmbH**, Stefan gestiona la parte financiera "
"de Ditana, mientras se centra exclusivamente en su desarrollo como "
"desarrollador independiente. Esta estructura garantiza una administración "
"transparente de los recursos de este proyecto impulsado por la comunidad."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thomas Zipproth"
msgstr "Thomas Zipproth"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Image src={thomas} alt=\"Thomas Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"
msgstr "<Image src={thomas} alt=\"Thomas Zipproth\" width={150} />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Thomas Zipproth is an experienced software developer from Mindelheim, "
"Germany, with deep expertise in image processing — particularly in document "
"scanning and recognition technologies. He has spent his career working on "
"high-precision systems for automated data extraction and provides valuable "
"testing support and feedback for Ditana, helping refine its usability and "
"reliability."
msgstr ""
"Thomas Zipproth es un desarrollador de software experimentado de Mindelheim "
"(Alemania), con amplios conocimientos en procesamiento de imágenes, en "
"particular en tecnologías de digitalización y reconocimiento de documentos. "
"Ha dedicado su carrera a sistemas de alta precisión para la extracción "
"automatizada de datos, y aporta a Ditana un valioso apoyo en las pruebas, "
"así como comentarios que ayudan a perfeccionar su facilidad de uso y su "
"fiabilidad."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
#, no-wrap
msgid "Acknowledgements"
msgstr "Agradecimientos"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Ditana would not be what it is without the contributions of others. Special "
"thanks to:"
msgstr ""
"Ditana no sería lo que es sin las contribuciones de otras personas. Un "
"agradecimiento especial a:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"**Alexey Melezhik** for the [Sparrow6](https://github.com/melezhik/Sparrow6) "
"work that replaced Ansible in 0.9.3 and for ongoing collaboration on test "
"infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"**Alexey Melezhik**, por el trabajo en [Sparrow6](https://github.com/"
"melezhik/Sparrow6) que sustituyó a Ansible en la 0.9.3 y por su colaboración "
"continua en la infraestructura de pruebas."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"**Ralf Hersel** of [gnulinux.ch](https://gnulinux.ch) for the early coverage "
"and the [podcast interview](https://gnulinux.ch/ciw119-podcast) that "
"introduced Ditana to a wider Swiss/German-speaking audience."
msgstr ""
"**Ralf Hersel**, de [gnulinux.ch](https://gnulinux.ch), por la cobertura "
"temprana y la [entrevista en su pódcast](https://gnulinux.ch/ciw119-podcast) "
"que dio a conocer Ditana a un público más amplio de Suiza y de habla alemana."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"Everyone who has filed an issue, sent feedback, or simply tried Ditana and "
"shared what worked or didn't."
msgstr ""
"Todas las personas que han abierto una incidencia, enviado comentarios o "
"simplemente probado Ditana y contado qué funcionó y qué no."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/who-we-are.mdx
msgid ""
"If you want to reach us: [support@ditana.org](mailto:support@ditana.org) for "
"anything at all, the [Discord channel](https://discord.gg/RgcdumdE9J) for a "
"conversation, and the issue trackers for [the installer](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-installer/issues), [the configuration](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-config/issues) and [the package pipeline](https://github.com/"
"acrion/ditana-build/issues) when you have something specific."
msgstr ""
"Si quiere ponerse en contacto con nosotros: [support@ditana.org]"
"(mailto:support@ditana.org) para cualquier cosa, el [canal de Discord]"
"(https://discord.gg/RgcdumdE9J) para conversar, y los gestores de "
"incidencias del [instalador](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-installer/"
"issues), de la [configuración](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/"
"issues) y de la [canalización de paquetes](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-"
"build/issues) cuando tenga algo concreto."
